# Turn a code review into a form on Android

A local Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct model answered two requests through the Hermes gateway (originally recorded in French on Android). The Android app reopened both replies from the conversation. The screenshots show the form it rendered, the changes it detected, and the choices it offered.

## Ask for a form

> Create a custom page titled “Submission Review” that I can pin to this discussion. I want a single form with two fields: the file name and the code-review point to verify. When I fill it out, let me review my request before sending it.

The first reply created the custom page with **File name** and **Review point** fields. **Prepare a draft…** builds an editable message, and **Pin to this discussion** keeps the form attached to the thread.

## Add a priority choice

> Keep both fields from my form. Add a priority choice to distinguish items to address today from items that can wait.

After the first form was pinned, the discussion offered **Open pinned tool** on the original reply and **Compare versions** on the revision.

<a href="examples/revue-des-remises/30-formulaire-modele-local.png"><img src="examples/revue-des-remises/30-formulaire-modele-local.png" width="300" alt="Trial form with empty filename and review-point fields, a draft action and a button to pin the form."></a>
<a href="examples/revue-des-remises/31-discussion-modele-local.png"><img src="examples/revue-des-remises/31-discussion-modele-local.png" width="300" alt="The conversation shows both requests, the pinned first form and the action to compare the revision."></a>

## Compare the two versions

The revision kept the same page and both field IDs. **Changes** shows one added required field, **Priority**. In **Proposed**, its menu offers **Today** and **Handle later**. You can inspect these choices before selecting **Use this version** or **Keep pinned version**.

<a href="examples/revue-des-remises/32-revision-modele-local.png"><img src="examples/revue-des-remises/32-revision-modele-local.png" width="300" alt="The changes tab lists the added priority field, its two options and the actions to adopt or keep a version."></a>
<a href="examples/revue-des-remises/33-priorite-modele-local.png"><img src="examples/revue-des-remises/33-priorite-modele-local.png" width="300" alt="The proposed form retains both original inputs and opens the priority choice menu."></a>

The phone displayed the original assistant messages `2` and `5` from this example conversation. Both reply texts matched the completed gateway runs byte for byte. The receipt contains the exact replies, model and build identifiers, and SHA-256 hashes for the four original captures. [Redacted capture receipt](examples/revue-des-remises/receipt.json)
